timestamp=2026-11-08T22:30:02.914Z level=INFO run=50327b16 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# Let us try to extract the full family tree structure as a graph.\n# Maybe parse the ASCII drawing? That can be complex. Alternatively,\n# look for parent-child relationships by analyzing the drawing patterns.\n# Common patterns: child appears below parent with connecting lines like | and + or \\ /\n\npath = '/app/dataset/genealogy_trees.txt'\nwith open(path, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    lines = f.readlines()\n\n# Let's look at the specific area around Dawid Majtyka more closely\n# Find line number containing Dawid Majtyka\nfor i, l in enumerate(lines[:]):\n    if 'Dawid Majtyka' in l:\n        # print surrounding lines\n        for j in range(max(0, i-10), min(len(lines), i+15)):\n            print(j+1, repr(lines[j]))\n        break\nelse:\n    print('not found')\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
