timestamp=2026-11-08T22:30:34.250Z level=INFO run=50327b16 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# Let us try to parse this more systematically. The drawing uses ASCII art.\n# In the drawing, a child is typically placed below parent with vertical lines connecting.\n# Look for Dawid Majtyka line and look at the column positions of the name box and nearby connectors.\npath = '/app/dataset/genealogy_trees.txt'\nwith open(path) as f:\n    lines = f.readlines()\n\nfor i, l in enumerate(lines):\n    if 'Dawid Majtyka' in l:\n        # Find the position of \"Dawid Majtyka\" in the line\n        pos = l.find('Dawid Majtyka')\n        print(f\"LINE {i+1}, pos={pos}\")\n        # look at line above - does it have | above the name area?\n        if i > 0:\n            print('ABOVE:', repr(lines[i-1]))\n        print('THIS:', repr(l))\n        if i < len(lines)-1:\n            print('BELOW:', repr(lines[i+1]))\n        break\nelse:\n    print('not found')\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
