timestamp=2026-11-08T22:31:20.331Z level=INFO run=50327b16 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# Looking at the line: Kazimierz and Dawid are next to each other, both in boxes.\n# And above in line 92, I see something like ... / ... \\ and also Tobiasz below in next lines\n# But we need to understand the parent-child relationships from the tree structure.\n# Let us look at the full tree in a different way - maybe the dataset is in a structured format?\n# Check if there might be a different representation (like a textual family tree format, GEDCOM-like, or just adjacency list in text)\npath = '/app/dataset/genealogy_trees.txt'\nwith open(path) as f:\n    full = f.read()\n\n# Maybe the tree is described as a DAG with edges like \"parent -> child\" or in some other format\n# Search for common patterns\nfor pattern in ['->', 'father of', 'parent of', 'child of', 'descendant', 'Dawid Majtyka:']:\n    if pattern in full:\n        print('FOUND:', pattern)\n        # show context\n        idx = full.find(pattern)\n        print(repr(full[idx-50:idx+100]))\n        break\nelse:\n    print('not found common patterns')\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
