timestamp=2026-11-08T22:51:02.979Z level=INFO run=50327b16 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# Now sum the account balances of their direct children who have more than one grandchild\n# Wait - the task says: \"sum the account balances of their direct children who have more than one grandchild\"\n# \"their\" refers to the great-great-grandparent (g2g). So the direct children of g2g are those candidates above.\n# But the task says \"their direct children...\" - we need to sum account balances of which people?\n# Let us read the task again carefully: \"Find the great-great-grandparent of 'Dawid Majtyka' in the family tree. Using the database, sum the account balances of their direct children who have more than one grandchild. Return only the final integer.\"\n# So for the great-great-grandparent (their), look at their direct children - but among those direct children, only those who have more than one grandchild. Sum account balances of those direct children (the children of g2g) - is that right?\n# Or sum balances of the grandchildren? Or sum balances of something else?\n# \"sum the account balances of their direct children who have more than one grandchild\" - the direct children are the ones being selected (who have >1 grandchild). So sum their (those children's) account balances.\n# That matches what we have: the list of children of g2g with >1 grandchild. So sum their account balances.\n\n# Now look up account balances in people_accounts.csv\n# We need to match names from the tree to names in the CSV. Names are \"first_name last_name\".\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
